# YouTube integration

## YoutubeApiFacade

- Single facade for YouTube Data API v3 — all external calls go here.
- Each method receives the **channel API key** (`setKey(apiKey)` on requests).
- Paginate with `nextPageToken`; expose page-level methods for quota-aware sync (`fetchUploadsPlaylistPage`, `fetchCommentThreadPage`, …).
- Log errors with channel/video id context; return last page on FORBIDDEN for search/comments.

## SyncVideoTask

- One **connected** channel per scheduled run (round-robin).
- One uploads-playlist page per run (`engage.sync.video.pages-per-run`, default 1); backfill continues via `nextPageToken` into older videos.
- Upsert videos by `youtubeId`; update channel `syncAt` and `nextPageToken`.

## SyncCommentsTask

- Process up to `engage.sync.comments.videos-per-run` videos due by `commentsSyncAt`.
- One comment page per video per run; store `commentsNextPageToken` until exhausted.
- Process top-level threads and replies; upsert by `youtubeCommentId`.

## Never

- Call YouTube API from endpoints or repositories.
- Hard-code or expose API keys in responses.
- Change scheduler intervals without noting quota impact in ARCHITECTURE.md.
